# A right-click on ↻ shows the reload menu (PR #517) in a split pane too. Its rows act on the focused
# page, so a right-click on the other pane's ↻ (shown while the pointer is over its bar) focuses that
# pane first: Force Refresh and Clear Cookies then reach the page that was right-clicked, not the one
# that had the focus. Before this, a split pane's ↻ had no menu at all.
pace 0.5
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true}

cra://debug?windowSize=1200x800
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=left
expect-log loaded 127\.0\.0\.1 \(HTTP 200\)
wait 1
cra://action/addSplitView
cra://navigate?url=${PAGE}?n=right
wait 2
cra://debug?paneLengths=start
expect-log pane lengths start: .* focused=1 horizontal$

# The unfocused pane: the menu, and that pane takes the focus and the commands.
cra://debug?paneReloadMenu=other&pane=0
expect-log pane reload menu other: menu=.*Force Refresh the Page.*Clear Cookies and Refresh.* focused=0 page=0$

# The focused pane: the menu, and the focus stays.
cra://debug?paneReloadMenu=focused&pane=0
expect-log pane reload menu focused: menu=.*Force Refresh the Page.*Clear Cookies and Refresh.* focused=0 page=0$
cra://debug?paneReloadMenu=back&pane=1
expect-log pane reload menu back: menu=.*Force Refresh the Page.* focused=1 page=1$
